      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "This article describes the complex anatomic structures that pass across the lateral aspect of the knee, particularly the iliotibial tract and the underlying anterolateral ligament and capsule. It provides data on their strength and roles in controlling tibiofemoral joint laxity and stability. These findings are discussed in relation to surgery to repair or reconstruct the anatomic structures, or to create tenodeses with similar effect."
      },
